  data: {
    LLM: "Learn the Mus hand rankings thoroughly. Understand when to say 'mus' for card exchange versus 'no hay mus' to begin betting. Manage your stone count carefully—don't risk too many stones on marginal hands.\n\nObserve opponent betting patterns to deduce hand strength. Bluff selectively in early phases to force opponents to fold. In the pares and juego phases, accurately assess whether your hand justifies seeing or raising.\n\nMaster the art of stone management. Sometimes it's better to fold and conserve stones than to risk elimination. Use position (being the mano) to control betting tempo. When low on stones, play more conservatively; when opponents are low, apply pressure.",
    Player: "Learn the Mus hand rankings thoroughly. Understand when to say 'mus' for card exchange versus 'no hay mus' to begin betting. Manage your stone count carefully—don't risk too many stones on marginal hands.\n\nObserve opponent betting patterns to deduce hand strength. Bluff selectively in early phases to force opponents to fold. In the pares and juego phases, accurately assess whether your hand justifies seeing or raising.\n\nMaster the art of stone management. Sometimes it's better to fold and conserve stones than to risk elimination. Use position (being the mano) to control betting tempo. When low on stones, play more conservatively; when opponents are low, apply pressure.",
